{
    "background_story": "Sierra was a free-spirited artist who lived in a small, coastal town. She was known for her bold and unconventional style, often challenging the status quo with her work. When the local government announced plans to demolish a historic lighthouse to make way for a luxury resort, Sierra was outraged. She saw the lighthouse as a symbol of the town's heritage and identity, and she was determined to save it. Inspired by the ancient Greek tragedy of Antigone, who defied the law to honor her brother, Sierra took a stand against the authorities. She organized protests, created powerful art installations, and rallied the community to join her cause. Despite facing opposition and criticism, Sierra remained steadfast in her convictions, ultimately helping to save the lighthouse and preserve the town's cultural heritage.",
